e","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ross Vasta","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10651","person_slug":"ross-vasta","vote":"no"},{"name":"Russell Broadbent","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10069","person_slug":"russell-broadbent","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sharman Stone","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10612","person_slug":"sharman-stone","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sharon Bird","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10043","person_slug":"sharon-bird","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sharon Grierson","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10266","person_slug":"sharon-grierson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Simon Crean","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10158","person_slug":"simon-crean","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sophie Mirabella","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10461","person_slug":"sophie-mirabella","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Smith","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10594","person_slug":"stephen-smith","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steve Gibbons","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10250","person_slug":"steve-gibbons","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steven Ciobo","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10122","person_slug":"steven-ciobo","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stewart McArthur","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10428","person_slug":"stewart-mcarthur","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stuart Henry","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10298","person_slug":"stuart-henry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sussan Ley","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10387","person_slug":"sussan-ley","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tanya Plibersek","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10513","person_slug":"tanya-plibersek","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Teresa Gambaro","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10239","person_slug":"teresa-gambaro","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Burke","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Smith","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10592","person_slug":"tony-smith","vote":"no"},{"name":"Warren Entsch","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10203","person_slug":"warren-entsch","vote":"no"},{"name":"Warren Snowdon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10599","person_slug":"warren-snowdon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Warren Truss","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10641","person_slug":"warren-truss","vote":"no"},{"name":"Wayne Swan","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10617","person_slug":"wayne-swan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wilson Tuckey","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10642","person_slug":"wilson-tuckey","vote":"no"}],"name":"Northern Territory National Emergency Response Bill 2007 - Consideration in Detail - Review and Racial Discrimination Act","noes":72,"question":"This division relates to the Policy _[For the NT National Emergency Response](/policies/36)_. The majority voted against [amendments](http://www.openaustralia.org/debate/?id=2007-08-07.89.1) introduced by Labor MP [Jenny Macklin](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Jenny_Macklin&mpc=Jagajaga&house=representatives), which means that they were rejected. The amendments were: _(1) Page 9, after clause 5 (after line 14) insert: 5A Review of operation etc of Part 4 The Minister must cause to be conducted, as soon as practicable after the first anniversary of the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent, a review of the operation and effectiveness of Part 4 (Acquisition of rights, titles and interests in land)._ _(2) Clause 132, page 93, (lines 12-17), omit subclauses (1) and (2), substitute:_ _(1) Subject to subsection (3), the provisions of this Act, and any acts done under or for the purposes of those provisions, are, for the purposes of the [Racial Discrimination Act 1975](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racial_Discrimination_Act_1975), special measures and are consistent with Part 2 of the Racial Discrimination Act 1975._ _(2) Subject to subsection (3), the provisions of this Act, and any acts done under or for the purposes of those provisions, are not laws as described by subsection 10(3) of the Racial Discrimination Act 1975._ Ms Macklin explained that amendment (1) would require a review to be conducted of the part of the bill that deals with the acquisition of rights, titles and interests in land, which relates principally to the new five-year leases over township areas and also the town camps.(Read Ms Macklin's full explanation [here](http://www.openaustralia.org/debates/?id=2007-08-07.88.1). ) Amendment (2) relates to the Racial Discrimination Act and reflects an amendment made earlier.(See that earlier amendment [here](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/division.php?date=2007-08-07&number=2&dmp=36&house=repr","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-404","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2007-08-07/3"}
